[516.670121, "o", "         VERIFIER · HUMAN  \r\nR1  CODE-READ (declared REPRODUCED)  medium    src/flask/sessions.py:96   NullSession blocks __setitem__/update/setdefault/etc. but not the in-place union operator, so `session |= {...}` on an app with no secret key silently mutates the null session and drops the data instead of raising the documented RuntimeError.                        "]
[516.670144, "o", "                                                                                    stands (codex)"]
[516.670164, "o", "    \r\nR2  CODE-READ (declared REPRODUCED)  high      src/flask/sessions.py:334  "]
[516.67019, "o", "open_session catches only BadSignature, but itsdangerous raises BadPayload (a sibling of BadSignature under BadData, not a subclass) when a correctly-signed cookie cannot be deserialized, so such a cookie propagates an exception out of session opening and turns every request from that client into a 500 instead of falling back to an empty session.  stands (codex)    \r\nR3  CODE-READ (declared REPRODUCED)  low       src/flask/sessions.py:193"]
[516.670214, "o", "  get_cookie_path is annotated `-> str` and documented to fall back to '/' when APPLICATION_ROOT is None, but it actually returns None, and werkzeug then emits the session cookie with no Path attribute, scoping it to the requesting URL's directory rather than the whole site.                                                                        "]
[516.670232, "o", "     stands (codex)    \r\nR4  CODE-READ                        low"]
[516.670249, "o", "       src/flask/sessions.py:354  A cookie rejected by open_session (bad signature or expired) produces a fresh session with modified=False, so save_session's deletion branch at line 354-355 never fires and the unusable cookie is never cleared from the client, which after a SECRET_KEY rotation without fallbacks leaves every client re-sending a dead cookie indefinitely.             stands (codex)    \r\nR5"]
[516.67027, "o", "  CODE-READ                        low       "]
[516.670286, "o", "src/flask/sessions.py:373  save_session calls get_signing_serializer(app) a second time and dereferences the result with only a type-ignore, so if app.secret_key becomes falsy between open_session and save_session the request dies with AttributeError on None rather than a meaningful error.                                                                                "]
[516.670299, "o", "       stands (codex)    \r\n"]
