[516.670526, "o", "\r\n    \r\n    src = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.getcwd(), \"src\"))\r\n    if not os.path.abspath(flask.__file__).startswith(src):\r\n        print(\"FAILED: imported flask is not the one under review:\", flask.__file__)\r\n        sys.exit(1)\r\n    print(\"flask under review:\", flask.__file__)\r\n    \r\n    app = Flask(__name__)\r\n    app.secret_key = \"k\"\r\n    app.config[\"APPLICATION_ROOT\"] = None   # docstring: '... or uses / if it is None'\r\n    p = app.session_interface.get_cookie_path(app)\r\n    print(\"get_cookie_path(app) ->\", repr(p), \"(declared return type is str)\")\r\n    if p is not None:\r\n        print(\"no defect: got\", repr(p))\r\n        sys.exit(1)\r\n    \r\n    sess = app.session_interface.session_class({\"a\": 1})\r\n    sess.modified = True\r\n    resp = app.response_class(\"ok\")\r\n    app.session_interface.save_session(app, sess, resp)\r\n    sc = resp.headers.getlist(\"Set-Cookie\")\r\n    print(\"Set-Cookie:\", sc)\r\n    if not sc:\r\n        print(\"no cookie was set at all\")\r\n        sys.exit(1)\r\n    if any(\"Path=\" in c for c in sc):\r\n        print(\"no defect: a Path attribute is present\")\r\n        sys.exit(1)\r\n    print(\"DEFECT CONFIRMED: get_cookie_path returned None despite its 'str' annotation and its\")\r\n    print(\"documented '/' fallback, and the session cookie is emitted with no Path attribute,\")\r\n    print(\"so the browser scopes it to the request's directory instead of the site root.\")\r\n    sys.exit(0)\r\n    PYEOF\r\n    PYTHONPATH=\"$ROOT/src\" \"$PY\" \"$ROOT/_repro_cookie_path.py\"\r\n"]
[516.670544, "o", "R3 — exit 1, output:\r\n    interpreter: /home/pdbethke/PycharmProjects/rip-monitor/venv/bin/python3\r\n    [stderr]\r\n    Traceback (most recent call last):\r\n      File \"/tmp/corral-review-2246427696/tree/_repro_cookie_path.py\", line 2, in <module>\r\n        import flask\r\n      File \"/tmp/corral-review-2246427696/tree/src/flask/__init__.py\", line 2, in <module>\r\n        from .app import Flask as Flask\r\n      File \"/tmp/corral-review-2246427696/tree/src/flask/app.py\", line 31, in <module>\r\n"]
[516.670563, "o", "        from . import cli\r\n      File \"/tmp/corral-review-2246427696/tree/src/flask/cli.py\", line 780, in <module>\r\n        class CertParamType(click.ParamType[t.Any]):\r\n                            ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~^^^^^^^\r\n    TypeError: type 'ParamType' is not subscriptable\r\nR3 — DEMOTED to CODE-READ: the script exited 1 — it did not demonstrate the claim\r\n\r\nverifier codex:\r\nI could not refute any finding. R1 follows from Werkzeug 3.1's inherited __ior__ bypassing NullSession.update. R2 correctly identifies an uncaught sibling exception. R3 accurately describes the explicit falsy-APPLICATION_ROOT case, although normal defaults avoid it. R4 and R5 both follow from reachable control-flow paths in save_session.\r\n\r\nR1 — STANDS: I traced NullSession's MRO and mutation guards. At src/flask/sessions.py:96, __ior__ is not rebound to _fail. Werkzeug 3.1's UpdateDictMixin.__ior__ delegates through super().__ior__, reaching dict.__ior__ rather than the overridden NullSession.update, so the inherited operation can mutate the object. The reviewer's failed environment setup does not undermine the code-level claim.\r\n"]
[516.670586, "o", "\r\nR2 — STANDS: At src/flask/sessions.py:331-335, only BadSignature is caught. BadPayload derives from BadData independently of BadSignature, and payload decoding happens after signature verification in itsdangerous. Therefore a validly signed but undecodable payload can escape open_session. I found no broader exception handler in this method that would convert it to an empty session.\r\n\r\nR3 — STANDS: The declared return at src/flask/sessions.py:187 is str, while line 193 returns SESSION_COOKIE_PATH or APPLICATION_ROOT with no final '/' fallback. If both values are falsy, including the finding's explicit APPLICATION_ROOT=None input, the result is None. Flask's default APPLICATION_ROOT='/' makes this uncommon but does not refute the named input or narrow the claim beyond its stated configuration.\r\n\r\nR4 — STANDS: A rejected cookie reaches src/flask/sessions.py:334-335 and creates an empty SecureCookieSession with its class-default modified=False. In save_session, lines 354-367 delete only when an empty session is modified, so this fresh session returns without deleting the rejected client cookie. I found no rejection flag or other deletion path connecting open_session to save_session.\r\n\r\nR5 — STANDS: The serializer obtained at src/flask/sessions.py:324 is not retained. For a nonempty session that must be saved, line 373 calls get_signing_serializer again and immediately invokes dumps. Since lines 303-305 return None for a falsy current secret key, changing app.secret_key during the request makes this dereference fail with AttributeError. The type-ignore affects static checking only and supplies no runtime guard.\r\n\r\nchecked and found sound:\r\n"]
[516.670603, "o", "  · get_signing_serializer key ordering: SECRET_KEY_FALLBACKS are extended first and app.secret_key appended last, which matches itsdangerous' convention of signing with the last key in the list while accepting all of them on load; the 'at top' comment is misleading but the behaviour is right.\r\n  · SecureCookieSession modification tracking for `|=`: werkzeug >= 3.1 (the pinned floor in pyproject.toml, line 29) implements UpdateDictMixin.__ior__ with @_always_update, so `session |= {...}` does set modified=True on a real session; only NullSession is affected (finding 1).\r\n  · NullSession's other mutation doors: __setitem__, __delitem__, clear, pop, popitem, update and setdefault are all bound to _fail; I checked the MRO (CallbackDict -> UpdateDictMixin -> dict, plus MutableMapping) and __ior__ is the only inherited mutator left unguarded.\r\n  · save_session's Vary handling: 'Cookie' is added when the session was accessed, when the cookie is deleted, and when the cookie is set; the only path that returns without adding it (should_set_cookie false) is a path where the response does not depend on the cookie.\r\n  · The empty-session branch: `if not session: if session.modified: delete_cookie(...)` correctly distinguishes 'never had a session' from 'session was emptied', and passes the same domain/path/secure/samesite/httponly/partitioned attributes used when setting, so the deletion matches the original cookie.\r\n"]
[516.670623, "o", "  · partitioned + secure interaction: werkzeug's dump_cookie forces secure=True whenever partitioned is set, so passing SESSION_COOKIE_PARTITIONED through without validating SESSION_COOKIE_SECURE does not emit an invalid Partitioned-without-Secure cookie.\r\n  · get_expiration_time and open_session's max_age are consistent: both derive from app.permanent_session_lifetime, so a permanent cookie's browser expiry and the server-side signature max_age agree.\r\n  · SignatureExpired is a subclass of BadTimeSignature -> BadSignature, so expiry is genuinely covered by the handler at line 334; only BadPayload/BadData escapes (finding 2).\r\n  · SecureCookieSession.__init__'s on_update closure signature matches CallbackDict's call convention (self.on_update(self)), so modification tracking fires on the guarded methods.\r\n  · _lazy_sha1 is used via staticmethod as digest_method and is only invoked inside itsdangerous at signing time, so hashlib.sha1 is not touched at import on FIPS builds as intended.\r\n  · is_null_session / make_null_session are honoured by the only save path I could find (src/flask/app.py:1415), so a NullSession is never serialized into a cookie.\r\n"]
[516.693893, "o", "\r\nledger: review entry 20260908T153928Z-review-2f925333c93a.json.gz written to .corral/ledger (signed by corral-certify)\r\n  adjudicate a finding: corral review adjudicate .corral/ledger 2f925333c93a#R1 --confirm|--refute --reason \"…\"\r\n"]
